{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/127537-getting-into-hunter-the-vigil-hopefully","id":127537,"title":"Getting into Hunter: The Vigil (Hopefully)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-07T09:37:15-07:00","id":127537,"title":"Getting into Hunter: The Vigil (Hopefully)","content":"<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Hello, everyone.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I\u2019m a long time GM and player, and my group has more-or-less consisted of the same people for about 25 years. Over the years we\u2019ve mainly stuck to our core game, WFRP1e, with Shadowrun, Call of Cthulhu, Vampire: The Masquerade (we played in the 90s), and some other stuff thrown in in between campaigns.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Currently, the group would like to do a Call of Cthulhu campaign set in the 1970s. The reasons for this are mainly because of the lack of ease of communication compared to current day (with cellphones, internet, etc.), but also because it\u2019s much more familiar-feeling than, say, the 1920s. It allows the players to feel comfortable with the setting while not streaming what they\u2019re seeing from Google Glass, or whatever.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">At any rate, the group prefers more of the \u201chunting\u201d aspect, even in CoC. They do enjoy the investigation but like to have the investigation culminate in some sort of climactic battle with them as participants, rather than just being witness to things, and ultimately, their characters going insane.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Also, they like subtle story development. Many of the published CoC adventures, for example, have Elder Gods showing up, even though the adventures themselves are one-offs. This makes no sense to me, and the group would rather follow a trail to a ghoul cult \u2014 unearthing mysteries and tangential plots (part of the fun is finding out whether or not what you\u2019re investigating pertains to what you\u2019re actually after) and have a battle with those forces than, say, seeing something from another dimension; the latter is far less relatable in a sense (yes, I know it\u2019s not supposed to be relatable for the characters, but lack of familiarity isn\u2019t fun for this player group), and summarily, far less impactful.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The players like playing their characters for a long time, and they like campaigns where they invest lots of time. Most sessions are 10am to 10pm, and we meet about twice a month. It\u2019s less than when were were younger (if we MISSED a weekend about 10 years ago, it was considered a bad month).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">At any rate, I\u2019d really like to run Hunter for this group, as I have had the core book for quite some time. Additionally, I have purchased the updated Armory book, The nWoD core book, and Slashers. Is there anything else that would come in handy?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">In addition to these questions, is there a place I can direct my players to on-line that give a breakdown of the different compacts, etc., and other information about the game? That is, when they ask, \u201cWhat\u2019s Hunter? How\u2019s it different? What kind of characters are available to play within the Hunter: The Vigil World?\u201d I\u2019d like to be able to direct them somewhere, even if the description is simple; some mystery can be quite helpful. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Thank you for your time.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2798-ordo-septenarius","name":"Ordo Septenarius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T10:48:59-07:00","id":127584,"title":"","content":"Mortal Remains just came out, and it updates the system to the new God-Machine Chronicle rules revision. Even if you don't intend to use those revisions, it's filled with new monsters, player powers, and hunter organizations. Very good book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T10:50:23-07:00","id":127586,"title":"","content":"My suggestion is to start by asking if they want to play alone against the world, with a large network of like minded contacts, or as part of a large organisation.<br /> <br /> Then play Tier 1, Loyalists of Thule, or VASCU - since those are the groups that best fit what you've said your group likes; in my humble opinion. Hunter orgs tend to be good ad investigation or combat, but there's nothing explicitly described as good at both, but I think those two will come in closer than others.<br /> <br /> <br /> There isn't really much online that I can think of that summarises Hunter. However the keyword I would say is diversity, you can play hunter as anything from manly men with shotguns fighting monsters to a group of teenagers wearing black and trying to become real witches. Every Compact and Conspiracy in the core book is practically a different game all by itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T11:12:48-07:00","id":127609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/127537-getting-into-hunter-the-vigil-hopefully?p=127584#post127584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortal Remains just came out, and it updates the system to the new God-Machine Chronicle rules revision. Even if you don't intend to use those revisions, it's filled with new monsters, player powers, and hunter organizations. Very good book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am trying to find a better description on the God-Machine Chronicles; is it absolutely necessary to play? What rules does it change?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2798-ordo-septenarius","name":"Ordo Septenarius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T11:45:59-07:00","id":127624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ordo Septenarius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/127537-getting-into-hunter-the-vigil-hopefully?p=127609#post127609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am trying to find a better description on the God-Machine Chronicles; is it absolutely necessary to play? What rules does it change?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vices and Virtues become free form, Morality is replaced with a sort of mental integrity, Combat has been updated significantly, a new system of status effects called conditions and tilts has been added, experience costs have been flattened, experience is now gained from more interesting sources, and a social conflict system was added. <br /> <br /> The rules update is free, by the way:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/114078.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\"> World of Darkness: God-Machine Rules Update - Onyx Path Publishing | World of Darkness (new) | Demon: The Descent | Chronicles of Darkness | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\"> http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> World of Darkness: God-Machine Rules Update - What Has Risen May Fall What is the God-Machine? That question doesn't have a single, easy answer, but that doesn't stop </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T12:21:02-07:00","id":127650,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much. Downloaded it and reading it now. To be clear, Mortal Remains was a replacement for the God-Machine Chronicles, which were a replacement for the nWoD rules-set? <br /> <br /> Will the books I have coming, such as &quot;Armory,&quot; etc., even be usable with all these changes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2798-ordo-septenarius","name":"Ordo Septenarius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T13:01:12-07:00","id":127677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ordo Septenarius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/127537-getting-into-hunter-the-vigil-hopefully?p=127650#post127650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you very much. Downloaded it and reading it now. To be clear, Mortal Remains was a replacement for the God-Machine Chronicles, which were a replacement for the nWoD rules-set?<br /> <br /> Will the books I have coming, such as &quot;Armory,&quot; etc., even be usable with all these changes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mortal Remains is not a replacement for the God-Machine Chronicles. The Appendix updates the core Hunter book to be compatible with the God-Machine, but you will still need the corebook to play. The books and supplements for Hunter will be useful to you; I can't see why they wouldn't be. (And welcome!) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T13:04:24-07:00","id":127682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ordo Septenarius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/127537-getting-into-hunter-the-vigil-hopefully?p=127650#post127650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you very much. Downloaded it and reading it now. To be clear, Mortal Remains was a replacement for the God-Machine Chronicles, which were a replacement for the nWoD rules-set?<br /> <br /> Will the books I have coming, such as &quot;Armory,&quot; etc., even be usable with all these changes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite, mortal remains is not a replacement for God-Machine Crhonicles, just update some rules of H:tV to match better with the new rules. My advice? (personal opinion, of course) Buy mortal remains only if you will use all the material (about, prometheans, sin-eaters, changelings, etc) and not only for the rules (it's not the main focus of the supplement).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2896-nemastoncito","name":"Nemastoncito","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T11:18:38-07:00","id":238356,"title":"","content":"If you want your game to become more Cthulhoid than buying the full GMC is not a bad idea. It deals with a giant machine which is trying to regulate everyone's life for reasons I can't tell you, because I would have to kill you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. No really, it's motivations are unknown. Slasher is imo the best book of the nWoD, so good buy on that one. The other books give you more info on either vampires, werewolves and mages/witches. Mortal Remains deals with the rest, changelings, mummies, prometheans (Frankenstein's monsters), demons and other thing I might forget. The Horror recognition guide is a really cool prop, but it's all fluff just like the vampire clanbooks.<br /> <br /> If you are mystery focused and you like the toolkit design of the nWoD, you might want to get your hands on Mysterious Places, Urban Legends or any other book out of the blue line. They all need work though. You must make everything your own, because they give mostly story seeds, which need to be fleshed out. I like to use the Book of Spirits, because it adds the entire Spirit World to your games. That books provides you with a setting, plus you can use spirits as an excuse for all the nasty things happening in a setting.<br /> <br /> Personally I would recommend getting Compacts and Conspiracies and the setting pdf Block by Bloody Block. Both add useful info and are cheap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T17:14:57-07:00","id":245703,"title":"","content":"I personally appreciated more Damnation City for Requiem than Block By Blood Block, but that's my personal opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T18:06:48-07:00","id":247305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/127537-getting-into-hunter-the-vigil-hopefully?p=245703#post245703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally appreciated more Damnation City for Requiem than Block By Blood Block, but that's my personal opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only use the chapters containing the districts, the sites and subjects. It's an unique book, but a lot of words for such a simple concept. In the end you only need a few residential area's (rich, poor, suburbs) an industrial area (or maybe a harbor) and a few commercial area's (both offices and nightlife/food service). You can also use a city model (Hoyt, Burgess, Ullmann) or Sim City 4 (residential, industrial, commercial office, commercial service) for building your city. I found the more robust BbbB method more to my liking.<br /> <br /> Just a tip: a good buy is the Haven City of Violence RPG. You can buy the pdf for $2 and it gives you a blueprint of a city covering all bases. It works with 6 district and each district has several neighbourhoods. I found the setup to be pretty much the same as any city there is. It covers all bases. The distinction between district and neighbourhood works really well. You can have a very poor neighbourhood in a very rich district for example. Just like Harlem in Manhattan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1873,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","user":"Jan Paparazzi","date":". 09-02-2014, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}